  "fitness": "undetermined",
  "outcome": "insufficient_information",
  "explanation": "The assessment scope is limited to hearing for a commercial driver licence. The guidelines establish an unconditional exclusion for unaided hearing loss ≥40 dB in the better ear and allow for a conditional licence if the standard can be met with a hearing aid, subject to periodic review and specialist input. However, the nurse note contains no audiometry results, no documentation of hearing aid use, and no assessment by an ENT specialist or audiologist regarding the patient's hearing status. While the note documents transient loss of consciousness and a visual field defect, these do not establish current hearing criteria. The absence of specific hearing data prevents the establishment of either the unconditional exclusion or the conditional permission prerequisites.","missing_information": ["Audiometry results (unaided thresholds in better ear)", "Confirmation of hearing aid use and aided thresholds", "Assessment by ENT specialist or audiologist regarding fitness to drive with/without aids"]}
